# Expected failures of scripts/validate/pjdfstest.sh in user mode: one line per check, `dir/file.t:N` followed by the detail from the log with the values that vary between runs normalised (NAME, INODE_A and so on, SERVER_UID, SERVER_GID; see tap.sh). Every entry sits under the reason that explains it; regressions are anything failing that is not listed here.
# The candidate list after a run is validation/results/pjdfstest/failed.txt; an entry with no reason is a bug to report, not a line to add. The reasons were attributed with scripts/validate/pjdfstest-nodev.sh (docs/validation.md): a failure that vanishes, or changes, when devices are replaced by regular files is a device cascade; one that persists has another cause.

# The server refuses block and character device nodes (S_IFBLK, S_IFCHR) with EPERM whatever its privilege. Each refused mknod is one failure, and the checks that then expect the device to exist cascade: ENOENT where the device should be; an EEXIST, ENOTDIR or ENOTEMPTY not raised because nothing or a directory is there; a rename or open denial in a sticky or read-only directory not raised because the target that should have been a device is missing, so only the directory permission is checked; the lstat that then finds the object at the wrong name; and the cleanup that follows. (214 checks)
